// A FLAG STANDS IN THE DOT COLUMN'S WAY, and a full-size note is not exempt.
//
// The augmentation dot of an UNBEAMED flagged note is pushed right of the FLAG whenever the
// flag's ink reaches the row the dot ended up on — LilyPond's Dot_column builds a rightward
// skyline over the column's supports (lily/dot-column.cc:100-141) and the flag is one of them.
// Until session 314 Lily# answered a flat "head ink right + one dot" for every full-size note
// and only the grace house held the ported rule, so three of these four went out 0.7632 short.
//
// MEASURED on LilyPond 2.26.0 (scratch/p314/flagdot-dump.ly dumps the NoteHead / Dots / Stem /
// Flag extents; each number is the dot's LEFT minus its own head's LEFT):
//   g8.  head ON A LINE, dot lifted one position   2.5174 = 1.2392 + 0.8282 + 0.4500
//   f8.  head IN A SPACE, dot not lifted           1.7542 = 1.3042          + 0.4500
//   g16. head ON A LINE                            2.5174
//   f16. head IN A SPACE                           2.5174  <- the 16th's flag is deeper
//                                                            (bottom -3.5502 against -3.0502),
//                                                            so it reaches even an unlifted dot
// where 1.2392 is the up stem's centre, 0.8282 the flag's own right edge, 1.3042 the black
// head's ink right and 0.4500 one dot width.
//
// The rests are BEAM BREAKERS, not decoration: Lily# auto-beams `g8. f8.` where LilyPond does
// not, and a beamed column has no flag at all — the first probe written for this
// (scratch/p314/dots.lys) measured nothing for exactly that reason and reported "no ink moved".
octave absolute
time 4/4

part v { }

section A {
  v {
    g8. r16 f8. r16 r2 |
    g16. r32 f16. r32 r2 r4 |
  }
}

form main { ~A }

score main { staff ~v }
